From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: secondary index inconsistent with primary

When database_openpackages is called and packages.db exists but
packagenames.db does not, database_table_secondary with DB_CREATE
would create an empty secondary index. This skips the legacy
translation, leaving the secondary index inconsistent with the
primary database. As a result, dists/ index files may not reflect
all packages after an update.

Fix by checking for this condition before opening the tables and
running database_translate_legacy_packages first.

See Debian bug #1095493.

---
 database.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

Index: reprepro/database.c
===================================================================
--- reprepro.orig/database.c
+++ reprepro/database.c
@@ -2190,6 +2190,25 @@ retvalue database_openpackages(const cha
 		return RET_ERROR;
 	}

+	/* If the packages database exists but the secondary index does not,
+	 * we need to translate the legacy format first. Doing this before
+	 * database_table_secondary avoids creating an empty secondary index
+	 * that would be inconsistent with the primary database.
+	 * (See Debian bug #1095493) */
+	if (!readonly) {
+		char *packages_filename = dbfilename("packages.db");
+		char *packagenames_filename = dbfilename("packagenames.db");
+		bool needs_migration = isregularfile(packages_filename) &&
+				!isregularfile(packagenames_filename);
+		free(packages_filename);
+		free(packagenames_filename);
+		if (needs_migration) {
+			r = database_translate_legacy_packages();
+			if (RET_WAS_ERROR(r))
+				return r;
+		}
+	}
+
 	r = database_table_secondary("packages.db", identifier,
 			dbt_BTREE, readonly?DB_RDONLY:DB_CREATE,
 			"packagenames.db", dbt_BTREEVERSIONS, &table);
